  RELAXED
  OFF
}

/// GTC-179 (E2, phase 2): the per-PERSON mark — Moment 4 §10.3, "a mark alongside the
/// recipient picker (go gentle / don't chase), set at Moment 1 or any time — a hosting
/// judgement the system stores and obeys". Founder Ruling 1, 2026-08-27: GENTLE is one
/// nudge at day 5; DONT_CHASE is none at all, on the direct path AND the proxy path
/// (Ruling 3).
///
/// TWO VALUES, NO "NORMAL" SENTINEL. NULL on the column carries "no mark", which is a
/// different fact from either mark and is what makes an unmarked person defer to the
/// event's pace. Same reasoning AttendanceAnswer records for having no PENDING.
///
/// ⚠ MIRRORS `NUDGE_MARK_OFFSET_DAYS` IN src/lib/nudge-cadence.ts — same
/// schema-follows-module direction, same reason. See NudgePace above.
///
/// NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR OPT-OUT (Do-Not-Touch Zone 7). This is a HOST-set preference
/// layered ON TOP of `Person.smsOptedOut`/`SmsOptOut`, which is GUEST-set and legally
/// binding. Every eligibility ladder must check opt-out FIRST and this second, so that
/// a host clearing DONT_CHASE can never resume messaging someone who opted out.
enum NudgeMark {
  GENTLE
  DONT_CHASE
}

/// GTC-189 rulings AH and AL — the chase's channel for a person with no usable mobile.
///
/// ONE ENUM, TWO COLUMNS: `Event.chaseWhenNoMobileDefault` (the default — NULL means NOT
/// SET) and `PersonEvent.chaseException` (the named exception — NULL means FOLLOW THE
/// DEFAULT). Sharing it is what makes the composition one total expression:
///
///   personEvent.chaseException
///     ?? event.chaseWhenNoMobileDefault
///     ?? DEFAULT_CHASE_WHEN_NO_MOBILE        // BY_EMAIL — ON, ruling AH
///
/// ⚠ NAMED VALUES, NOT A BOOLEAN, AND THAT IS THE POINT. This control's polarity inverted
/// on 2026-09-15: under ruling AG the per-person control meant CHASE THIS ONE, and under
/// ruling AH it means HAND THIS ONE TO ME. A boolean could be read either way, so a field
/// name, a comment or a test label about it would read perfectly well while meaning the
/// opposite, and would not announce itself in a diff. The founder's one-line check is that
/// anything describing the control as "tick to chase" was written under AG and is now
/// backwards. Every value here names its own behaviour, so a read cannot invert.
///
/// TWO VALUES, NOT ONE, because ruling AL rules BOTH directions: default ON plus
/// HAND_TO_HOST means she takes him, and default OFF plus BY_EMAIL means he is chased.
///
/// ⚠ ITS COMPOSITION RULE IS NOT `NudgePace`/`NudgeMark`'s, a few lines above, and copying
/// the neighbour is the obvious move and the wrong one. THE NAMED EXCEPTION WINS. The
/// founder's reason is on `PersonEvent.chaseException`.
enum ChaseWhenNoMobile {
  BY_EMAIL
  HAND_TO_HOST
}

